            <ArticleTitle>[The role of coronary angioplasty in the treatment of ischemic cardiopathy. 1 of 2 parts].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>151-70, 104</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Since its introduction in 1977, coronary angioplasty has gained wide acceptance and is now the primary treatment of coronary artery disease in properly selected patients. In this article the authors review the technique, current indications, contraindications, results and complications of coronary angioplasty.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
